## Parity (web components/a11y/VisuallyHidden.tsx → native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web file is an anonymous a11y utility ("sr-only"): no data fetch, no charts/
maps, no i18n literals of its own (it renders caller-provided children). Its three
documented modes are reproduced as idiomatic SwiftUI:
  • default `.sr-only`           → VisuallyHidden(text): 1pt, hit-test-disabled,
                                   exposed to VoiceOver via accessibilityLabel.
  • liveRegion + aria-live       → liveRegion:true posts AccessibilityNotification
    (polite|assertive) + aria-atomic   .Announcement on text change / on appear;
                                   polite→.default, assertive→.high speech priority;
                                   .updatesFrequently trait.
  • focusable skip-link          → VisuallyHiddenSkipLink: @FocusState, invisible
    (focus:not-sr-only)            until focused then revealed (TS tokens, reduce-
                                   motion honored), stays in focus order.
  • element-polymorphic `as`     → View.visuallyHidden(exposedToAssistiveTech:)
    + children                     modifier wraps arbitrary content.
Tokens P1/S9: Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSAnimation.
Strings P1/S10: per-surface table "VisuallyHidden" (VisuallyHidden.strings) — no
  English literal in code.
Telemetry P1/S11: view.opened with stable slug "VisuallyHidden" via OSLog seam.

## States (web source has NO data states — faithfully reproduced)
  empty (blank/whitespace content → nothing announced, a11y-hidden),
  hidden (default sr-only), live-region polite, live-region assertive,
  focusable hidden (unfocused) ↔ revealed (focused). No loading/error/stale/
  offline branches exist in the web source, so none are invented (covenant #2/#5).

